# Build context exclusions for the vendored shell image.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, and it is not tidiness.
#
# The Dockerfile installs dependencies from `package-lock.json` and then does
# `COPY . .`. With no exclusions that second step copies the HOST's
# `node_modules` (330 MB) straight over the tree npm just installed, so the
# image ships whatever happened to be on the machine that ran the build rather
# than what the lockfile pins. It also copies the host's `dist/`, so a stale
# local build can end up served if anything later goes wrong.
#
# Both were true when this image was first built and verified: the running
# container served a bundle that did not match the source in the same commit,
# which is the specific failure that makes "I checked it renders" worthless.
#
# `git check-ignore` already refuses both paths — they were simply never
# refused to Docker, and the two ignore files are not the same mechanism.
node_modules
dist

# Nothing below is needed to build, and each one either bloats the context or
# invalidates the cache on every commit.
.git
.gitignore
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
test
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
